**What was built** (UE 5.8.3, T1000, all original/procedural — no AI slop, no copyrighted assets):

- **The island**: lighthouse (tapered tower + glowing lamp room + rotating warm beam), 4 duty stations, shipping lane, shore, 3 story notes, 6 wreck slots, 6 physical reefs, volumetric storm fog, sun arc, day/night lighting.
- **The job is the story** — every mechanic has weight: **lens → beam range** (salt decays it nightly; fog cuts reach 35%), **oil → storm survival** (burn scales with fury; short oil = the light dies mid-night), **wrecks → your choice**: salvage for oil (unreported) or report to the chart — unreported wrecks age into **reefs that later sink ships**. The island remembers, physically.
- **The record decides the ending**: every duty, omission, salvage, report, and loss is logged (auditable in-game via Tab, on disk as JSON). 5 ending tiers — **all 5 fired live in testing**: DARK TAKES THE ISLAND (-20), SEA STOPS TRUSTING THE LIGHT (-16), BARELY AFLOAT, THE LIGHT HELD (18), KEEPER SUPREME (33→91), THE FULL TRUTH (103: 30 saved / 0 lost / 3 notes / 0 dark nights).
- **Audio**: 7 SFX synthesized with studio v3 real DSP (storm bed, beam hum, dark drone, ship bell, salvage clank, page blip, hull crack) — beds swap when the light dies.
- **Menu + settings**: title screen, volume, subtitles, camera distance (day-one accessibility per ground [299af5f81d60]).
- **Diegetic tutorial**: the previous keeper's checklist coaches cycle 1.
- **Demo autoplayer** doubles as the keeper-record demo and regression harness (`KL_DEMO=1`).

**Critic scores per round** (binding = lower of self/qa-critic):
- Round 1: 8.2 / 7.8 → **7.8** (audio missing, no menu, proxy visuals) → ranked fixes
- Round 2: 8.9 / 8.6 → **8.6 PASS** (audio + menu + visual pass landed)
- Round 3: polish confirmed, FULL TRUTH 103 reproduced, 0 errors → **8.6 held**

**Verified by running it**: 13 full/partial sessions, pawn spawn + input proven, save/load atomic, clean quit path, screenshots (day/night-beam/ending) captured each round.

**Honest gaps**: keeper character is the TP template pawn (no custom mesh); no human hands-on playtest yet (demo-driven); path-erosion memory is design-noted, not built.

